137Glu)","cdna":"c.410G>A","protein":"p.Gly137Glu","genomic":"","zygosity":"heterozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"missense","key":"V1"},{"gene":"ESRRG","as_reported":"c.446A>G (p.Lys149Arg)","cdna":"c.446A>G","protein":"p.Lys149Arg","genomic":"","zygosity":"heterozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"missense","key":"V2"},{"gene":"ESRRG","as_reported":"c.539G>A (p.Cys180Tyr)","cdna":"c.539G>A","protein":"p.Cys180Tyr","genomic":"","zygosity":"heterozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"missense","key":"V3"},{"gene":"ESRRG","as_reported":"c.550C>T (p.Arg184Cys)","cdna":"c.550C>T","protein":"p.Arg184Cys","genomic":"","zygosity":"heterozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"missense","key":"V4"},{"gene":"ESRRG","as_reported":"c.1346T>G (p.Leu449Arg)","cdna":"c.1346T>G","protein":"p.Leu449Arg","genomic":"","zygosity":"heterozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"missense","key":"V5"},{"gene":"ESRRG","as_reported":"c.1352dup (p.Leu451Phefs∗38)","cdna":"c.1352dup","protein":"p.Leu451Phefs*38","genomic":"","zygosity":"heterozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"frameshift","key":"V6"}],"variant_roles":["causal","causal","causal","causal","causal","causal"],"segregation":"mostly de novo","inheritance":"AD","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":true,"quotes":["We clinically describe eight individuals from seven unrelated families having heterozygous, mostly de novo variants in ESRRG: c.410G>A (p.Gly137Glu), c.446A>G (p.Lys149Arg), c.539G>A (p.Cys180Tyr), c.550C>T (p.Arg184Cys), c.1346T>G (p.Leu449Arg), and c.1352dup (p.Leu451Phefs∗38).","All individuals have motor developmental delay, muscular hypotonia, and eye movement disorders, as well as congenital ataxia or gait imbalance. Other symptoms include joint hyperflexibility, dysarthria, myopia, and growth delay."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AD","genotype_reason":"single heterozygous variant; mode as stated for the family"}],"notes":[{"id":"N:41265451:1","pmid":"41265451","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"Bresack et al. (2025) reported that all of the ESRRG variants they identified were absent from gnomAD (v4.1), predicted deleterious in silico, and located in intolerant segments of the protein. Molecular modeling suggested the variants reduce protein function.","inheritance":"AD","quotes":["All identified variants are absent in gnomAD (v.4.1), are in silico deleterious, and are located in intolerant segments of the protein.","Molecular modeling of the identified variants suggests a reduction in protein function."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:41265451:2","pmid":"41265451","section":"gene_function","statement":"Bresack et al. (2025) found that knocking out ESRRG in HEK293T cells significantly increased cell proliferation. Overexpressing wildtype ESRRG restored normal proliferation, but overexpressing the patient variants did not. All variants localized correctly to the nucleus, yet each significantly reduced transcriptional activity in an ERR response element (ERRE) reporter assay.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["ESRRG knockout resulted in a significantly increased proliferation rate in ESRRG-knockout HEK293T cells. Overexpression of wild-type ESRRG restored cell proliferation, while overexpression of the identified variants did not.","Despite the correct nuclear localization of all identified variants, the reporter gene assay revealed a significant reduction in transcriptional activity for all identified variants."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:41265451:3","pmid":"41265451","section":"description","statement":"Bresack et al. (2025) noted that ESRRG has the highest mutational constraint of the ESRR paralogs. On the basis of their clinical, molecular, and functional data, they implicated ESRRG in a dominant non-progressive congenital movement disorder with ataxia.","inheritance":"AD","quotes":["Among its ESRR paralogs, ESRRG exhibits the highest mutational constraint, yet it remains unlinked to a defined disease phenotype.","Given the acquired clinical, molecular, and functional data, we implicate ESRRG in the etiology of a non-progressive congenital movement disorder with ataxia."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]}],"dropped":{"records":[],"notes":[]},"gene_decisions":{"candidates":["ESRRG"],"confirmed":["ESRRG"],"dropped":[],"not_confirmed":[]},"candidate_inheritance":["AD"]}